{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791045550,"nonce":"laXKaPYwuvCEA7xgjuKRNfhtd3s=","title":"A concrete scalar passed to a Null\u003cT\u003e parameter of an inline function reads as null","message":"Rows: Issue3094, Issue4842 (`isNull(i)` with `i:Int = 0`, UInt, Int64.make(0,0) is true).\nThe call-boundary gate in ir/mir/helpers/signatures.rs `maybe_materialize_for_call` now boxes a\nconcrete scalar for a `Null\u003cT\u003e` formal, but these rows still fail: the call is inlined, and the\ninliner substitutes the raw argument for the `Null\u003cT\u003e` parameter. A bare `T` formal also gives true\nfor `isNullT(0)` (erased i64 compared with 0).","files":null}]}